(1. The purpose of this Report is to confirm, so far as reasonably practicable, whether or not the electrical installation is in a satisfactory condition for continued service) Tj
T* (\(see Section 5\). The Report should identify any damage, deterioration, defects and/or conditions which may give rise to danger.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 7 Tf
8.0499999999999989 TL
0. g
0. Tc
39.6850393700787407 670.6774015748030706 Td
(2. The person ordering the Report should have received the 'original' Report and the inspector should have retained a duplicate.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 7 Tf
8.0499999999999989 TL
0. g
0. Tc
39.6850393700787407 653.6695275590550409 Td
(3. The 'original' Report should be retained in a safe place and be made available to any person inspecting or undertaking work on the electrical installation in the) Tj
T* (future. If the property is vacated, this Report will provide the new owner/occupier with details of the condition of the electrical installation at the time the Report was) Tj
T* (issued.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 7 Tf
8.0499999999999989 TL
0. g
0. Tc
39.6850393700787407 619.6537795275589815 Td
(4. Where the installation incorporates a residual current device \(RCD\) there should be a notice at or near the device stating that it should be tested six-monthly. For) Tj
T* (safety reasons it is important that this instruction is followed.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 7 Tf
8.0499999999999989 TL
0. g
0. Tc
39.6850393700787407 594.1419685039369369 Td
(5. Section 4 \(Extent and Limitations\) should identify fully the extent of the installation covered by this Report and any limitations on the inspection and testing. The) Tj
T* (inspector should have agreed these aspects with the person ordering the Report and with other interested parties \(licensing authority, insurance company, mortgage) Tj
T* (provider and the like\) before the inspection was carried out.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 7 Tf
8.0499999999999989 TL
0. g
0. Tc
39.6850393700787407 560.1262204724408775 Td
(6. Some operational limitations such as inability to gain access to parts of the installation or an item of equipment may have been encountered during the inspection.) Tj
T* (The inspector should have noted these in Section 4.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 7 Tf
8.0499999999999989 TL
0. g
0. Tc
39.6850393700787407 534.614409448818833 Td
(7. For items classified in Section 7 as C1 \('Danger present'\), the safety of those using the installation is at risk, and it is recommended that a skilled person or persons) Tj
T* (competent in electrical installation work undertakes the necessary remedial work immediately.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 7 Tf
8.0499999999999989 TL
0. g
0. Tc
39.6850393700787407 509.1025984251967884 Td
(8. For items classified in Section 7 as C2 \('Potentially dangerous'\), the safety of those using the installation may be at risk and it is recommended that a skilled person) Tj
T* (or persons competent in electrical installation work undertakes the necessary remedial work as a matter of urgency.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 7 Tf
8.0499999999999989 TL
0. g
0. Tc
39.6850393700787407 483.5907874015747439 Td
(9. Where it has been stated in Section 7 that an observation requires further investigation \(code FI\) the inspection has revealed an apparent deficiency which may) Tj
T* (result in a code C1 or C2, and could not, due to the extent or limitations of the inspection, be fully identified. Such observations should be investigated without delay.) Tj
T* (A further examination of the installation will be necessary, to determine the nature and extent of the apparent deficiency \(see Section 6\).) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 7 Tf
8.0499999999999989 TL
